# Do not drive-by edit README.md

Repo root **`README.md`** is updated in a **dedicated explicit pass**, not while
you work on code in `src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, or elsewhere.

## Default rule

**Do not** open, edit, or “sync” `README.md` unless the current ticket
**explicitly** says to update the README.

This includes:

- “while I’m here” summary updates after API changes
- adding new features or analyses to the README bullet lists
- refreshing links or badges “for consistency”
- rewriting the introduction to match code you just changed

## What to do instead

| Need | Where |
|---|---|
| Public API detail | Docstrings on the implementation |
| User guides / recipes | `docs/` (MkDocs), when the ticket includes docs |
| Architecture / dev notes | `docs-dev/` |
| Deferred README work | Note in `docs-dev/codex_tickets/` report |

## When README.md *is* in scope

Only when the ticket title or instructions **explicitly** call for a README
update — typically after `src/` and public API work is finalized.

## Scope

This rule is for repo root **`README.md`** only.

Other files may be in scope when the ticket says so, including `README-DEV.md`,
`src/*/README.md`, and `docs/`.

## Relationship to AGENTS.md

Full policy: `AGENTS.md` → **`README.md` (STRICT)**. When they conflict,
`AGENTS.md` wins.
